   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to legalizing, validating, ratifying and confirming certain\ntransportation contracts of the Corning city school district",
    "basePrintNo": "S6671",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6671-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6671\n\nSPONSOR: O'MARA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to legalizing, validating, ratifying and confirming\ncertain transportation contracts of the Corning city school district\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would correct a clerical error between the Corning-Painted\nPost Area School District and the State Education Department in the\n2017-18 school year\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Legalizes, validates, ratifies, and confirms transportation\ncontracts for the 2017-18 school year.\n\nSection 2: Directs the Department of Education to consider the aforemen-\ntioned contracts for transportation aid.\n\nSection 3: Sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill seeks to mitigate the negative impact to the Corning-Painted\nPost School District which would lose a major portion of its State aid\ndue to a clerical error on the part of the district, which results in\nthe loss of transportation aid.\n\nWithout the restoration of the Transportation Aid, the school district\nwould be faced with either cutting the quality and scope of its educa-\ntional programs or raising real property taxed dramatically.  This would\nplace an undue burden on their residents and present hardships to many\nin their community.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
